\ boot.fam — the kernel's main (docs/OS.md): what the node image does when
\ tabernacle hands it the machine.  Built after src/kernel.fam as bin/img
\ (scripts/build.sh), the image tabernacle is patched for.
\
\ Every hart the machine has is started first (hstart: each other hart's
\ stacks come from the heap, before the pages are counted).
\
\ Memory, from the bottom: the image; the stdlib's return-id stack and
\ variables; the kernel's heap (the other harts' stacks, and 64 KiB kept for
\ what it takes before the pages are counted); the pages, up to 0x87F00000;
\ hart 0's data stack below 0x87FF0000; the stdlib's guard page; the harts'
\ mailboxes (0x87FF1000); hart 0's loop-frame stack above them.

trapinit
hstart
gp@ 10000 lit + FFF lit + FFFFF000 lit and
87F00000 lit pginit
"kernel: " puts nharts @ u. nharts @ 1 lit = if " hart, " else " harts, " then puts
pgfree# dup u. " pages free (" puts 8 lit rshift u. " MiB)" puts
0A lit putc
tmrinit
begin wfi 0 lit until
